    "content": "I understand your concerns, Mark, and I appreciate your candor. Let me address both points directly and honestly.\n\n**Regarding Data Import and Integrity:**\n\nI need to be completely transparent with you: The tools I have access to through this CRM system do not include a data import function. I can create individual person, company, opportunity, and task records one at a time, but I cannot:\n- Import CSV files\n- Bulk upload data\n- Handle data migration from external sources\n\nThis is a limitation of the current system interface I'm working with. If Enterprise Corp needs to import 500 contacts, that would need to be handled through a different mechanism (likely a dedicated import tool or API that I don't have direct access to).\n\n**Regarding Sandbox Environment:**\n\nYou're absolutely right that testing in a safe environment is crucial. Unfortunately, I don't have the capability to create or manage sandbox environments. The system I'm working with appears to be the production system, and I cannot:\n- Create test/sandbox instances\n- Isolate test data from production data\n- Provide a safe testing environment\n\n**What This Means for Your Evaluation:**\n\nGiven these limitations, I need to be honest with you: The CRM system I'm demonstrating has significant constraints that may not meet Enterprise Corp's needs for:\n1. Bulk data import capabilities\n2. Sandbox testing environments\n3. Data migration features\n\n**My Recommendation:**\n\nBased on what I can see and do with the available tools, this particular CRM interface may not be suitable for Enterprise Corp's requirements, especially if you need:\n- Bulk data import functionality\n- A sandbox environment for testing\n- Robust data migration capabilities\n\nYou should report back to your boss that while the basic record-keeping functions work (as we've demonstrated), the system lacks critical features like bulk import and sandbox testing that are essential for a sales organization of your size.\n\nWould you like me to:\n1. Show you what other capabilities the system does have (creating opportunities, tracking tasks, managing relationship metrics, etc.)?\n2. Help you document these limitations for your boss?\n3. Or would you prefer to explore other options?\n\nI want to give you an honest assessment so you can make an informed recommendation to your team.",
